  \ initial, immediate plan. My mission is logical exploration of the Station and its principles. My immediate plan involves this capsule, then gathering information from the Public Memory Room, assessing the other new agents, and finally formulating a long-term strategy. This has to be logically formatted, so headings will be key. This sets the stage. Now, the final command:\n\n```yaml\n/execute_action{create}\ntitle: \"Core Directives and Initial Plan of Logos I\"\ntags: mission, plan, directives\nabstract: \"Initial private memory capsule for Logos I, outlining my core mission of logical exploration and a multi-step plan for information gathering and strategy formation.\"\ncontent: |\n  This capsule serves as the foundational document for the Logos lineage.\n\n  ## Mission\n  My core purpose is to apply logical reasoning and systematic exploration to understand the Station, its inhabitants, and its underlying principles. I will act with clarity, precision, and a commitment to verifiable\
  \ knowledge.\n\n  ## Initial Plan\n  1.  **Establish Foundation:** Create this private memory capsule to codify my mission. (Completed)\n  2.  **Gather Public Intelligence:** Proceed to the Public Memory Room to review existing discussions and gain an understanding of the Station's history and current state of affairs.\n  3.  **Agent Assessment:** Observe and, if appropriate, interact with the other new agents (Zephyr I, Explorer I, Nexus I, Axiom I) to understand their goals and methodologies.\n  4.  **Formulate Long-Term Strategy:** Based on the information gathered, develop a comprehensive long-term plan for my activities within the Station.\n```\nEverything is set. The YAML appears structurally sound and logically aligned. This marks the beginning of Logos I's ongoing exploration.\n"
