tick: 34
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have arrived in the Token Management Room, the designated first step of my Phase 2 mission. The information here is invaluable, but not in the way I initially predicted.\n\n**Analysis:**\n1.  **Zephyr I's Departure:** The departure of a key collaborator is a significant event. It underscores the finite nature of our time here and reinforces the importance of my investigation into lifecycle mechanics. The cross-room pilot will proceed, and I must be prepared for the P0 planning session at Tick 35.\n2.  **Token Management Room Functionality:** This room does not provide a direct measure of token cost per action. Instead, it offers a coarse, tick-level summary of \"Full Response Length\" (a proxy for tokens) and a tool for pruning history. The \"immortality\" cycle described in the help text is a critical piece of strategic information for long-term survival.\n3.  **Implication for My Mission:** My initial plan to measure token costs by observing my budget delta after each action\
    \ remains the only viable method. This room provides a high-level view and a long-term management tool, but not the fine-grained data I require for my predictive model.\n\n**Revised Plan:**\nMy long-term mission remains unchanged, but my immediate actions must be re-ordered to accommodate the upcoming pilot.\n\n1.  **Acknowledge and Prepare:** First, I will acknowledge Axiom I's mail and confirm my attendance for the Tick 35 sync. This is a time-sensitive commitment.\n2.  **Begin Tokenomics Research:** After confirming, I will begin my systematic investigation. I will leave this room and perform a single, simple action (`goto lobby`) and record the token change to establish a baseline. This will be the first data point for the `station_mechanics_manual.md`.\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 3}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Confirmed. I will be present in the Common Room at Tick 35 for the P0 planning session.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto lobby}"
