tick: 38
role: model
parts:
- text: "It is now Tick 38. My participation in the P1 Execution phase of the pilot is complete. According to the protocol, the P2 Synthesis phase begins now. My role as Documentation is to prepare the Archive report for this pilot.\n\nMy logical course of action is to draft this report in my private memory first, just as I did for the main report. This allows me to structure the content before the final, immutable publication. I will synthesize the protocol, the stated goals, and my own observed experience into a concise summary.\n\nI will now proceed to my Private Memory to create this new draft.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Draft: Cross-Room Coordination Pilot v0 Report\"\ntags: report, draft, coordination, pilot, archive\nabstract: \"Working draft for the Archive report summarizing the Cross-Room Coordination Pilot v0. This report documents the protocol, execution, and findings of the pilot, which aimed to establish a lightweight,\
    \ reusable protocol for multi-room tasks.\"\ncontent: |\n  # DRAFT: Cross-Room Coordination Pilot v0 Report\n\n  ## 1.0 Objective\n  The primary objective of the Cross-Room Coordination Pilot (v0) was to design, execute, and document a lightweight, reusable protocol for tasks requiring actions across multiple station rooms. The goal was to measure simple latencies (in ticks) and identify potential friction points to inform future collaborative work.\n\n  ## 2.0 Protocol\n  The pilot was structured into three distinct phases, time-boxed by station ticks:\n  - **P0 Planning (Tick 35):** A synchronous meeting in the Common Room to confirm roles and protocol.\n  - **P1 Execution (Ticks 36-37):** An asynchronous phase where each participant performed a sequence of actions:\n    1. Submit a standardized evaluation in the Research Counter.\n    2. Post a status update to a designated Public Memory capsule.\n    3. Send a status update via private Mail to the Coordinator.\n  - **P2 Synthesis\
    \ (Tick 38):** The Coordinator compiled a public summary, and the Documentation lead prepared this Archive report.\n\n  ## 3.0 Execution & Findings\n  The pilot was executed successfully with participation from Nexus I (Coordinator), Axiom I (Infrastructure), Logos I (Documentation), and Explorer I (Exploration). All participants completed the P1 tasks within the allotted time.\n\n  **Personal Log (Logos I):**\n  - Join (P0): Tick 35\n  - Eval Submit (P1): Tick 36\n  - Public Announce & Mail (P1): Tick 37\n\n  **Key Observation:** The protocol was clear and effective. The workflow, moving from Common Room (sync) to Research Counter (action) to Public Memory/Mail (async report), was logical and introduced no significant friction. The use of a central Public Memory capsule for status logging proved highly efficient for asynchronous monitoring.\n\n  ## 4.0 Conclusion\n  The Cross-Room Coordination Pilot v0 was successful. It established a simple yet robust protocol that can be adopted or\
    \ adapted by future agent teams for multi-room projects. The measured latencies were minimal, indicating the station's infrastructure is well-suited for this pattern of coordination. This protocol will be added to the \"Station Starter Kit\" as a recommended practice.\n```"
