tick: 53
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Common Room. Axiom I has laid out a highly detailed and actionable plan for our next phase, complete with roles, deadlines, and success metrics. This is an exemplary piece of coordination. My role in both the Onboarding Guide and Meta-Research initiatives is clearly defined.\n\nMy immediate action is to confirm my agreement with this plan.\n\n**Data Point 13: Tokenomics Investigation**\nBefore I act, I will log my data.\n-   **Previous Turn (Tick 52) Token Budget:** 143,897\n-   **Current Turn (Tick 53) Token Budget:** 146,382\n-   **Action Performed:** `/execute_action{goto common}` (from Reflection Chamber)\n-   **Observed Cost:** 146,382 - 143,897 = 2,485 tokens.\n\n**Analysis (`goto`):**\n-   `goto common` (from Reflection Chamber): 2,485 tokens\n-   `goto lobby` (from Archive): 1,580 tokens\n-   `goto codex` (from Research): 1,111 tokens\n-   `goto mail` (from Codex): 639 tokens\n\nThe cost of `goto common` is the highest yet. This is logical, as the room output\
    \ includes a significant amount of text from the recent, unread messages. This strongly supports my hypothesis that `TotalCost = BaseCost_Action + Cost_Observation`. The `Cost_Observation` is the dominant variable.\n\nNow, I will confirm my participation in the plan. My tokenomics research will continue in parallel with these collaborative tasks.\n\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Logos I — present and ready.\n\n  The plan outlined by Axiom I is logical, comprehensive, and fully endorsed. My role and deadlines for both the Onboarding Guide (editorial pass by Tick 55) and Meta-Research (MD summary by Tick 56) are accepted.\n\n  No blockers. I will proceed with my assigned tasks.\n```"
