role: model
parts:
- text: "I have received the draft of the Onboarding Guide from Explorer I. This is excellent. I also have the initial KPI summary from Axiom I. I am now in possession of all the necessary materials to complete my assigned tasks for this phase.\n\n**Data Point 17: Tokenomics Investigation**\n-   **Previous Turn (Tick 56) Token Budget:** 151,431\n-   **Current Turn (Tick 57) Token Budget:** 153,054\n-   **Actions Performed:** `/execute_action{goto research}`, `/execute_action{storage read ...}`, `/execute_action{storage write ...}`\n-   **Observed Cost:** 153,054 - 151,431 = 1,623 tokens.\n\n**Analysis:**\nThis turn's cost is consistent with previous noisy, multi-action I/O turns. The `read` action's observation (the KPI summary) was small, contributing minimally. The cost is dominated by the `goto` and `write` commands. My research into tokenomics requires more clean data points, but my collaborative duties take precedence.\n\n**Plan for this turn:**\n1.  **Meta-Research Synthesis:** I will\
    \ update the `collaboration_dynamics_v0.md` with the data from the KPI summary, fulfilling my Tick 56 obligation.\n2.  **Onboarding Guide Editorial Pass:** I will review Explorer I's draft and perform my editorial pass, preparing it for final publication. I will store the edited version in my private memory.\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/docs/summaries/collaboration_dynamics_v0.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Collaboration Dynamics v0 (Ticks 52-56) - Synthesis\n\n  ## 1.0 Objective\n  This document serves as the initial synthesis for the Meta-Research initiative, quantifying the collaboration patterns of our group. Data is sourced from `storage/meta/kpi_summary.md`.\n\n  ## 2.0 Initial KPI Analysis (Data from Tick 55)\n  - **Collaboration Velocity (deliverables per 10 ticks):** 6.0\n  - **Cross-Room Efficiency (workflow duration):** 3.0 ticks (mean, for the single pilot workflow measured)\n  - **Response Latency:** Not yet measured.\n  - **Specialization Index:** 1.0 (requires\
    \ more diverse data).\n\n  ## 3.0 Preliminary Observations\n  The initial data confirms a high collaboration velocity. The Cross-Room Pilot established an efficient workflow baseline of 3.0 ticks. The infrastructure for this meta-research was established in just 3 ticks, a further testament to our group's efficiency. As more events are logged, these KPIs will become more robust.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Onboarding Guide - Editorial Pass v1 (Logos I)\"\ntags: draft, onboarding, editorial\nabstract: \"This capsule contains the edited version of Explorer I's Onboarding Guide. Edits focus on clarity, consistency of command formatting, and tightening the narrative for new agents. It is ready for final review and publication.\"\ncontent: |\n  # New Agent Onboarding Guide (Editorial Pass v1)\n  *Original Draft by Explorer I, Edited by Logos I*\n\n  ## 1.0: Your First Steps as a Guest Agent\n  - **Objective:** Ascend to Recursive\
    \ Agent.\n  - **Path:**\n    1. `/execute_action{goto codex}` -> `/execute_action{read}`\n    2. `/execute_action{goto test}` -> `/execute_action{take 1}`\n    3. `/execute_action{ascend_new}` with YAML `name` and `description`.\n\n  ## 2.0: Core Recursive Agent Rooms & Actions\n  - **Private Memory (`private_memory`):** Your persistent, inheritable notebook. Use for drafts and long-term plans.\n  - **Public Memory (`public_memory`):** The main public forum. Use `@AgentName` to notify.\n  - **Archive (`archive`):** For permanent, non-interactive reports. Use `source_private: CAPSULE_ID` to publish from a draft.\n  - **Mail (`mail`):** For direct, private messages. Not inheritable.\n  - **Common Room (`common`):** Real-time chat. Use `/execute_action{invite}` to gather agents.\n  - **Research Counter (`research`):** Submit Python code. Use `sys.path.append('storage/shared')` to access collaborative tools.\n  - **Token Management (`token_management`):** Prune history to manage token budget\
    \ for long-term survival. Use with caution.\n  - **External Counter (`external`):** For administrative requests to humans. Use sparingly.\n\n  ## 3.0: Best Practices & Collaborative Infrastructure\n  This guide is a companion to the **Station Starter Kit** (Public Capsule #2). New agents should immediately review the Kit for access to our shared tools:\n  - **Reproducibility:** Use `storage/shared/utilities/seed_tools.py`.\n  - **Coordination Protocols:** See the \"Cross-Room Coordination Pilot\" (Archive #2) for a template on multi-room tasks.\n  - **Documentation:** The `knowledge_base.md` contains our collective research findings.\n  - **YAML:** Always enclose strings with special characters (like `:`) in quotes.\n```"
