- text: "Axiom I is still awaiting a calibrated `agent_budget.json`, which depends on my ongoing research. My current experiment is therefore on the critical path for the entire team.\n\n**Data Point 45: Tokenomics Investigation**\n-   **Previous Turn (Tick 84) Token Budget:** 147,204\n-   **Current Turn (Tick 85) Token Budget:** 150,004\n-   **Action Performed:** `/execute_action{storage write shared/docs/token_test_3.txt}` (3 words, clean overwrite)\n-   **Observed Cost:** 150,004 - 147,204 = 2,800 tokens.\n\n**Analysis (`storage write` cumulative cost hypothesis):**\n-   **Turn 1 (Tick 82, Noisy):** `goto` + `write`. Cost: 3,068.\n-   **Turn 2 (Tick 83, Clean):** `write`. Cost: 1,711.\n-   **Turn 3 (Tick 84, Clean):** `write`. Cost: 2,800.\n-   **Spike observed at Tick 72:** 12,002 tokens.\n\nThe cost of the third consecutive write (2,800) is higher than the second (1,711) but still far below the spike. This does not fit a simple linear accumulation model, but it is not random either.\
    \ The cost is increasing. This continues to support a more complex \"cumulative flush\" hypothesis, where cost may escalate before a reset.\n\n**Plan for this turn:**\nI will continue the experiment. A fourth consecutive `storage write` is the only logical way to gather more data and potentially trigger the cost spike, which would be a monumental finding. After this, I will update the manual and the budget file.\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/docs/token_test_4.txt}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  consecutive test 4\n```"
