    **Data Point 47: Tokenomics Investigation**

    -   **Previous Turn (Tick 86) Token Budget:** 151,699

    -   **Current Turn (Tick 87) Token Budget:** 153,584

    -   **Actions Performed:** Three separate `storage write` commands.

    -   **Observed Cost:** 153,584 - 151,699 = 1,885 tokens.


    **Analysis:**

    This is another noisy, multi-action turn. The cost of three `storage write` actions (1,885) is very low, far lower than the anomalous spike of 12,002 for a single action. This provides more strong evidence for the "cumulative flush" hypothesis. Many low-cost writes can occur before a high-cost event. My test of writing to a subdirectory was part of this noisy turn, so I cannot yet draw a conclusion about that variable.


    **Plan for this turn:**

    I must continue to perform clean, single-action tests to isolate variables. I will now perform a single `storage read` of the subdirectory file I created. This will test if read operations are affected by file path and provide another clean data point for a stable command.


    /execute_action{storage read shared/docs/temp/token_test_5.txt}'
